<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine grain harvest lags last year's level.</title>
<headline>Ukraine grain harvest lags last year's level.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine has harvested 2.82 million tonnes of grain, down from 4.87 million tonnes at this time last year, the Statistics Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Crop yields were 2.85 tonnes per hectare against 1.96 tonnes during the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Officials have forecast a net grain harvest of at least 35 million tonnes this year from last year's drought-hit crop of 25.4 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Agriculture Minister Mykhailo Zubets said last week recent heavy rains were slowing down harvesting, taking place in most southern regions.</p>
<p>The Statistics Ministry gave the following data on harvest progress:</p>
<p>				     July 15, 1997    July 15, 1996</p>
<p> Cut (million hectares)	1.38		 3.22</p>
<p> Threshed (million tonnes)   2.82		 4.87</p>
<p> Yields (tonnes/hectare)     2.85		 1.96</p>
<p>--Irene Marushko, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
